# Engineering

Stack: React, TypeScript, Vite, plain CSS custom properties, Zod, and Vitest. Commit the lockfile. No UI kit and no analytics SDK. Fonts may be vendored and bundled. Do not load them from a CDN at runtime.

- Keep screens free of DMRC JSON. Map responses in `src/lib/dmrc/` onto types in `src/lib/transit/`.
- Prefer local component state and pure functions. Add a same-origin adapter only if a real browser request from this app cannot read the API.
- That adapter may call fixed DMRC operations only. It rejects arbitrary URLs, sets timeouts and size limits, and does not forward cookies or spoof the official origin.
- Cancel stale search requests. Deduplicate identical in-flight requests.
- Store text size, theme, saved trips, and the chosen origin and destination locally. A refresh keeps that selection. If storage fails, the trip planner still works.
- "View route on map" shows that ride: the colored route and the marked stations, scrolled into view. Changing the tab alone is not enough.
- A street map uses Leaflet only after `station_code` coordinates are saved. Do not invent latitude or longitude. Gate exits appear only when a saved record names the gate and where it comes out.
- Do not add empty-state sentences such as "Your route will show here."
- Ride facts use an icon and a label on one row. Do not stack direction and platform as separate text blocks, and do not repeat the stop count in a second wording.
- Do not add `.env` until a real setting exists. Never commit secrets.

```ts
// Missing fare stays unknown. It is not zero.
const fare = typeof payload.fare === "number" ? payload.fare : null;
```
